    "narrative": "For August 24, our offensive engine is centered on **Corbin Carroll** (74.65) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23), who represent the highest-floor assets in the daily rotation. **Corbin Carroll** is a mandatory start; despite facing a capable arm in Kevin Gausman, the combination of a high-leverage batting order position (#2) and Gausman\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which elevates **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s stolen base probability to 86%\u2014creates an elite environment for category accumulation. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly, whose xERA of 5.27 invites a high-scoring outcome. We are also tracking **Max Muncy** (61.65) closely; while the platoon split against Zebby Matthews is minorly negative, the 10% park factor and the potential for a stolen base against a slow-moving battery make him a \"Strong\" play despite the mid-order slotting.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's slate involved **Griffin Conine** (35.12), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While his underlying metrics\u2014specifically his 0.383 xwOBA\u2014are encouraging, the disadvantage of a lefty-on-lefty matchup against Ranger Suarez and a bottom-of-the-order placement rendered him a \"Below floor\" option. We are prioritizing the higher output of **Mickey Moniak** (57.96) instead, whose dynamic platoon advantage against Cade Cavalli (+14%) outweighs the risk posed by Cavalli\u2019s stuff. **Zach McKinstry** (41.67) remains in the lineup by the slimmest of margins, buoyed largely by favorable wind conditions (+5%) that should assist his power profile, though he carries the highest volatility risk of our starters given the matchup against Drew Rasmussen. \n\nManagers should remain alert for final lineup confirmation, as all listed scores assume historical batting order placements. **Josh Naylor** (46.99) is currently positioned as a \"Marginal\" start; facing a high-tier arm like Zack Wheeler carries significant risk (-19% SP Skill), and he is the most likely candidate to be downgraded should defensive replacements or lineup shifts force him into a less advantageous spot. With **Trevor Story** and **Brice Turang** unavailable, our bench depth\u2014including **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014is restricted, meaning any late-breaking weather or lineup changes in the evening games could necessitate a quick pivot to preserve our remaining game caps.",
